# THE COMPOSED LAYERS THAT OWE NO SUM, AND FOR WHICH QUANTITY. One row per (composed layer,
# ground), carrying which ground it was and which quantity it lifts.
#
# ⛔⛔⛔ READ `quantity` BEFORE YOU USE THIS. NULL means EVERY quantity is suspended (nobody
#    searched at all); a value means exactly that quantity is (the overlap was found and could
#    not be sized against it). A caller computing one quantity's sum wants
#    `quantity IS NULL OR quantity = '<that one>'`. Claim "no sum at all" here while the second
#    arm pins `demand` and drops the column, and the claim is true of one arm and false of the
#    other with nothing downstream able to tell.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THIS RELATION EXISTS BECAUSE OF DE MORGAN AND IT IS WORTH SAYING WHY. The condition
#    it replaces was written as a conjunction of two negations, in two different SQL idioms,
#    at two call sites -- an `IS DISTINCT FROM` beside a `NOT EXISTS`. That is the most
#    drift-prone shape there is: two ways to say NOT, neither of which names what is being
#    excluded. `NOT a AND NOT b` is `NOT (a OR b)`, so the thing to name is the DISJUNCTION:
#    the fusions that are suspended. The callers then anti-join one relation, and adding a
#    third ground for suspension is a new file rather than a new clause in two predicates.
#
# ⛔ RUN THIS ALONE BEFORE READING ANY COMPOSITION CHECK. Every row here is a fusion whose
#   arithmetic is not owed, and a checker reporting a pass on one of these rows is reporting
#   about nothing.
# ⛔⛔⛔ THIS IS A BAG AND NOT A SET, WHICH IS THE WHOLE REASON IT IS TWO FILES. One fusion can
#    be suspended on more than one GROUND -- `every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity` files
#    both an unsearched elimination and an unsized conversion -- and it is suspended ONCE. The
#    key here is (composition, composed_layer, quantity, suspended_because); the key a caller
#    almost always wants is the first three, and `composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc` is that
#    projection.
#
# ⚠️ AND THE DIFFERENCE IS INVISIBLE TO ALMOST EVERY CALLER, WHICH IS WHY IT NEEDS SAYING.
#    `EXISTS`, `NOT EXISTS` and `EXCEPT` are blind to multiplicity: a duplicate row changes
#    nothing they compute. A `LEFT JOIN` is not, and a law that COUNTS fusions is not. So the
#    projection is what a counter or a joiner reads, and this file is what a reader who needs
#    the reason reads. A relation nobody has joined on is a multiplicity nobody has checked.
-- the three filings that lift the sum rule, one row per GROUND, carrying the quantity it lifts.
:union(ALL eliminations/unsearched.sqlc, eliminations/unsized.sqlc,
           composition/unsized_conversions.sqlc)
